# Cloudflare reads this file from the export root. It kept working when the app
# left Pages for a Worker: wrangler keeps `_headers` out of the asset manifest
# and uploads it as a deployment module, so the rules below still apply.
#
# The Matrix crypto WebAssembly module is served from a fixed path with no
# content hash in it — unlike the JS bundles, which Metro fingerprints — because
# the app has to know the URL to hand to `initAsync()` before it can load
# anything. A long cache on a mutable URL would mean a browser keeping one
# deploy's 7.8 MB module forever, so this one file revalidates instead: the
# ETag makes a repeat visit a conditional request, not another download.
/matrix_sdk_crypto_wasm_bg.wasm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The Matrix delegation files have no extension, so nothing infers a type for
# them and they would go out as octet-stream. The spec asks for JSON, and a
# federating server that cannot parse the answer falls through to the SRV
# record — which does not exist here.
#
# `not_found_handling = "single-page-application"` in `../wrangler.toml` sends
# unmatched paths to index.html, but real assets are matched first, so these
# files win. They did not exist until recently, which is why that path used to
# answer 200 with HTML.
/.well-known/matrix/server
  Content-Type: application/json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/.well-known/matrix/client
  Content-Type: application/json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
